# Keep .env files out of Docker images. The root .env and any nested
# .env file (e.g. apps/api/.env, services/*/.env) must never be baked
# into a published image — they typically contain DATABASE URLs with
# passwords, API keys, and operator secrets. Configure secrets via the
# container orchestrator's secret store instead. .env.local is excluded
# for the same reason; .env.example is intentionally allowed so the
# example file ships with the image.
.env
**/.env
.env.local
